> *How many potions are you bringing around? Potions that are immediately
> useful should be quaffed immediately, like gain level and gain ability.

The difference between an uncursed potion of gain ability and a
blessed potion is too large to drink it immediately; I'd wait and
bless them first to get the significant (six times) better result.

Gain level gives you skill slots and a few HP's/Pw pts.; I think
experience levels are most useful for spell casting (or being
admitted to the quest), and as a spellcaster I would level up,
otherwise not if I actually don't need additional skill slots.
Potions of gain level are also very useful for alchemy; might be
advantageous to save one for a stack of extra healing to be dipped
into.

